# =====================================================================
# Sparrow SMS credentials — example / template.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to `sms.properties` (same folder, no ".example")
#   2. Replace the placeholder values with the token + sender identity
#      you got from https://sparrowsms.com
#   3. Rebuild the project (Build → Build Project) so the new file
#      lands in target/classes
#
# HOW TO GET CREDENTIALS:
#   1. Sign up at https://sparrowsms.com
#   2. Purchase SMS credits (a bulk package or pay-as-you-go)
#   3. From your dashboard, copy the API token
#   4. Sparrow will email you the "sender identity" they've registered
#      for your account (during trial this is usually the string "Demo")
#
# SECURITY:
#   - `sms.properties` is git-ignored — it will NEVER be committed.
#   - This `.example` file is safe to commit; it contains no secrets.
#   - For production hospital deployment, prefer environment variables:
#         SPARROW_SMS_TOKEN=xxxx
#         SPARROW_SMS_FROM=MyClinic
#
# FALLBACK BEHAVIOR:
#   If this file is missing OR the token is blank, the app automatically
#   falls back to the console SMS simulator — no error, no crash.
#   You'll see a "SMS mode: CONSOLE" banner at startup so it's obvious.
# =====================================================================

sparrow.token=YOUR_SPARROW_API_TOKEN_HERE
sparrow.from=Demo
